<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>
@page { size: 8.5in 11.0in; margin: 0.6in 0.6in 0.6in 0.6in; }
body { font-family: "Segoe UI", Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #1E293B; line-height: 1.35; }
h1 { font-size: 16pt; color: #0F172A; border-bottom: 2px solid #1D4ED8; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 14px; }
h2 { font-size: 13pt; color: #1E3A8A; margin-top: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #CBD5E1; padding-bottom: 2px; }
h3 { font-size: 11pt; color: #1E40AF; margin-top: 10px; }
h4 { font-size: 10pt; color: #334155; margin-top: 8px; }
table { width: 490pt; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8px 0; font-size: 8.5pt; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; }
th { background-color: #1E3A8A; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; text-align: left; padding: 5px 6px; border: 1px solid #94A3B8; word-wrap: break-word; }
td { padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #CBD5E1; vertical-align: top; word-wrap: break-word; }
pre { background-color: #F8FAFC; border: 1px solid #CBD5E1; padding: 6px; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 8pt; white-space: pre-wrap; word-wrap: break-word; }
code { font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: 8.5pt; background-color: #F1F5F9; padding: 1px 3px; }
ul, ol { margin-top: 4px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style></head><body>
<h1>Job 5 Specification: mccaWriteOffFlatFileJob (MCCA Month-End Write-Off Flat File Export Job)</h1>
<h2>1. Executive Summary &amp; Job Overview</h2>
<table>
<tr>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Details</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Job Name / ID</b></td>
<td><code>mccaWriteOffFlatFileJob</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Source System</b></td>
<td><b>MCCA Database (<code>MCCA_WRITE_OFF</code> table in AlloyDB)</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Schedule / Frequency</b></td>
<td>Monthly (Month-End run on the 28th of the month at <code>11:00 PM</code> with parameter <code>batchDate=YYYYMMDD</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Spring XML Configs</b></td>
<td><code>jobs/mccaWriteOffFlatFileJob.xml</code> (<code>&lt;batch:job id=&quot;mccaWriteOffFlatFileJob&quot;&gt;</code>), <code>common/writeOffFlatFileBeanInfo.xml</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Source Database Table</b></td>
<td><code>MCCA_WRITE_OFF</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Output Flat File</b></td>
<td><code>${writeOff.flatfile.path}/MCCAWriteOffExport_${batchDate}.txt</code> (Comma-delimited <code>.txt</code> export file with 4 fields per line)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Java Components</b></td>
<td><code>WriteOff.java</code> (DTO), <code>WriteOffFlatFileMapper.java</code> (<code>RowMapper&lt;WriteOff&gt;</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Email Notification</b></td>
<td><code>writeOffMail</code> (<code>MailImpl.java</code> — runs in Step 2 after flat file generation)</td>
</tr>
</table>
<h2>2. End-to-End Architecture &amp; Step Execution Flow</h2>
<p><code>mccaWriteOffFlatFileJob</code> executes <b>2 sequential steps</b>:</p>
<pre>[Step 1: createFlatFileStep]
       │ (Executes writeOffJdbcCursorReader on MCCA_WRITE_OFF filtered by SUBSTR(:batchDate, 0, 6)
       │  -&gt; Formats fields via WriteOffFlatFileMapper.java
       │  -&gt; Writes comma-delimited lines to MCCAWriteOffExport_&lt;batchDate&gt;.txt via writeOffFlatFileItemWriter)
       ▼
[Step 2: writeOffMailStep] (MailImpl.java)
       │ (Sends email notification confirming Write-Off flat file generation)</pre>
<h2>3. Detailed Step-by-Step Business Logic, Formatting Rules &amp; SQL Query</h2>
<h3>Step 1: createFlatFileStep (writeOffFlatFileBeanInfo.xml &amp; WriteOffFlatFileMapper.java)</h3>
<h4>3.1 Input SQL Query (writeOffJdbcCursorReader)</h4>
<p>Reads all write-off transactions from <code>MCCA_WRITE_OFF</code> whose <code>SUBMITTED_DATE</code> year-month (<code>YYYYMM</code>) matches the first 6 characters of the job parameter <code>batchDate</code> (<code>#{jobParameters[&apos;batchDate&apos;]}</code>):</p>
<pre>SELECT
    CARRIER_CLM_NUM,
    COVERAGE_TYPE,
    WRITE_OFF_AMOUNT,
    WRITE_OFF_TYPE,
    SUBMITTED_BY,
    TO_CHAR(SUBMITTED_DATE, &apos;MMYYYY&apos;) AS SUBMITTED_DATE
FROM MCCA_WRITE_OFF
WHERE TO_CHAR(SUBMITTED_DATE, &apos;YYYYMM&apos;) = SUBSTR(:batchDate, 0, 6)
ORDER BY WRITE_OFF_SEQ_ID;</pre>
<p>*(In AlloyDB PostgreSQL, <code>SUBSTR(:batchDate, 1, 6)</code> is used as <code>SUBSTR</code> is 1-indexed in PostgreSQL, whereas Oracle treats <code>0</code> and <code>1</code> identically).*</p>
<h4>3.2 Field Formatting &amp; Padding Rules (WriteOffFlatFileMapper.java)</h4>
<p><code>WriteOffFlatFileMapper</code> applies exact fixed-width padding and decimal scaling rules to each row returned by the query:</p>
<table>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Database Column</th>
<th>Java Property (<code>WriteOff.java</code>)</th>
<th>Formatting / Padding Rule in <code>WriteOffFlatFileMapper.java</code></th>
<th>Included in Output File?</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>1. Claim Number</b></td>
<td><code>CARRIER_CLM_NUM</code></td>
<td><code>claimNumber</code></td>
<td>Right-padded with spaces to <code>9</code> characters (<code>%-9s</code>), or truncated to first <code>9</code> characters if <code>length &gt; 9</code>:<br/><code>String.format(&quot;%-9s&quot;, claimNumber)</code></td>
<td><b>Yes</b> (Field 1)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>2. Coverage Type</b></td>
<td><code>COVERAGE_TYPE</code></td>
<td><code>coverageType</code></td>
<td>Trimmed string (e.g., <code>&quot;PIP&quot;</code>)</td>
<td><b>Yes</b> (Field 2)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>3. Write-Off Amount</b></td>
<td><code>WRITE_OFF_AMOUNT</code></td>
<td><code>amount</code></td>
<td>1. Rounded to 2 decimal places (<code>#.00</code>).<br/>2. Multiplied by <code>100</code> to remove decimal point (cents representation, <code>Math.round(amount * 100)</code>).<br/>3. If <code>amount &gt;= 0</code>: Left-padded with leading zeroes to <b>11 digits</b> (<code>%011d</code>, e.g., <code>123.45</code> -&gt; <code>&quot;00000012345&quot;</code>).<br/>4. If <code>amount &lt; 0</code>: Prefix <code>&quot;-&quot;</code> followed by 10 zero-padded digits (<code>&quot;-&quot; + %010d</code>, total length 11, e.g., <code>-123.45</code> -&gt; <code>&quot;-0000012345&quot;</code>).</td>
<td><b>Yes</b> (Field 3)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>4. Write-Off Type</b></td>
<td><code>WRITE_OFF_TYPE</code></td>
<td><code>writeOffType</code></td>
<td>Trimmed string</td>
<td><b>Yes</b> (Field 4)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>5. Submitted By</b></td>
<td><code>SUBMITTED_BY</code></td>
<td><code>userId</code></td>
<td>Right-padded with spaces to <code>5</code> characters (<code>%-5s</code>), or truncated to first <code>5</code> characters if <code>length &gt; 5</code></td>
<td>Mapped on DTO (<code>BeanWrapperFieldExtractor</code> extracts the 4 fields below)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>6. Submitted Date</b></td>
<td><code>TO_CHAR(SUBMITTED_DATE, &apos;MMYYYY&apos;)</code></td>
<td><code>submittedDate</code></td>
<td>6-character string <code>MMYYYY</code></td>
<td>Mapped on DTO</td>
</tr>
</table>
<h4>3.3 Output Flat File Specification (writeOffFlatFileItemWriter)</h4>
<p>- <b>Output Path</b>: <code>file:${writeOff.flatfile.path}/MCCAWriteOffExport_#{jobParameters[&apos;batchDate&apos;]}.txt</code></p>
<p>- <b>Line Aggregator</b>: <code>DelimitedLineAggregator</code></p>
<p>- <b>Delimiter</b>: Comma (<code>,</code>)</p>
<p>- <b>Extracted Fields (<code>BeanWrapperFieldExtractor</code>)</b>:</p>
<p>```xml</p>
<p>&lt;property name=&quot;names&quot; value=&quot;claimNumber,coverageType,amount,writeOffType&quot; /&gt;</p>
<p>```</p>
<p>- <b>Sample Output Line</b>:</p>
<p>```text</p>
<p>JA159278 ,PIP,00000012345,WO</p>
<p>```</p>
<h3>Step 2: writeOffMailStep (MailImpl.java)</h3>
<p>Sends a completion email via <code>JavaMailSender</code> with the configured <code>writeOff.mail.from</code>, <code>writeOff.mail.to</code>, <code>writeOff.mail.subject</code>, and <code>writeOff.mail.body</code>.</p>
</body></html>
